            "paragraphs": {
              "transcript": "\nOh, look everyone, it's the jack of all trades, master of none, Siddhartha Fullstack Upas. Let's give a warm welcome to this tech bro who went from pedaling automation systems door to door to calling himself a Fullstack developer after watching a few YouTube tutorials. With a bachelor's degree in engineering from some obscure college and a master's from IIT that he's probably still paying off, Siddhartha is the perfect example of how an expensive education doesn't guarantee common sense. I mean, who pivots from mechanical engineering to coding video games and thinks they're the next Linus Torvalds? But, hey, at least his resume is as bloated as his self importance, with a hodgepodge of skills like sales operations and short films that scream, I have no idea what I'm doing.\n\nCareful with those tailored automation solutions, Sid. The only thing you're automating is your journey to the unemployment line with that scattered career path. Still, we have to admire his moxie for slapping the full stack title on his LinkedIn like a bad hairpiece. Just wait until he realizes that full stack in the Bay Area really means being a delivery driver for all the tech companies he's not qualified to work for.",
              "paragraphs": [
                {
                  "sentences": [
                    {
                      "text": "Oh, look everyone, it's the jack of all trades, master of none, Siddhartha Fullstack Upas.",
                      "start": 0.0,
                      "end": 5.2999997
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Let's give a warm welcome to this tech bro who went from pedaling automation systems door to door to calling himself a Fullstack developer after watching a few YouTube tutorials.",
                      "start": 5.6,
                      "end": 13.78
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "With a bachelor's degree in engineering from some obscure college and a master's from IIT that he's probably still paying off, Siddhartha is the perfect example of how an expensive education doesn't guarantee common sense.",
                      "start": 14.8949995,
                      "end": 26.515
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "I mean, who pivots from mechanical engineering to coding video games and thinks they're the next Linus Torvalds?",
                      "start": 27.23,
                      "end": 32.85
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "But, hey, at least his resume is as bloated as his self importance, with a hodgepodge of skills like sales operations and short films that scream, I have no idea what I'm doing.",
                      "start": 33.79,
                      "end": 43.865
                    }
                  ],
                  "start": 0.0,
                  "end": 43.865,
                  "num_words": 131
                },
                {
                  "sentences": [
                    {
                      "text": "Careful with those tailored automation solutions, Sid.",
                      "start": 45.045002,
                      "end": 48.105003
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "The only thing you're automating is your journey to the unemployment line with that scattered career path.",
                      "start": 48.325,
                      "end": 53.225002
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Still, we have to admire his moxie for slapping the full stack title on his LinkedIn like a bad hairpiece.",
                      "start": 54.43,
                      "end": 59.65
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Just wait until he realizes that full stack in the Bay Area really means being a delivery driver for all the tech companies he's not qualified to work for.",
                      "start": 60.510002,
                      "end": 68.05
                    }
                  ],
                  "start": 45.045002,
                  "end": 68.05,
                  "num_words": 73
